;; ral macOS Seatbelt rules for `net: true`, appended by
;; `core/src/sandbox/macos.rs::build_profile` and by nothing else.
;;
;; Seatbelt has no per-address network rules, so the socket half is one
;; wholesale allow.  The Mach half is here rather than in the base
;; profile because these daemons are exactly the network: configd
;; answers "what are the proxies and the DNS servers", the dnssd port
;; is the resolver's, and trustd evaluates TLS chains.  Under
;; `net: false` a hostname therefore cannot carry bytes out even as a
;; query label, at both layers at once.
;;
;; `com.apple.trustd`, not `com.apple.SecurityServer`: chain evaluation
;; without the keychain — see the base profile's mach-lookup comment.

(allow network*)

(allow mach-lookup
  (global-name "com.apple.SystemConfiguration.configd")
  (global-name "com.apple.dnssd.service")
  (global-name "com.apple.trustd")
  (global-name "com.apple.trustd.agent"))
